# Compare sky-layer clouds, a local storm cloud, box mist, global haze and a density-grid fog sphere.
# Select a Cloud/Fog entity for its shape and bounds; open its volume material for optical properties.
# Shapes and transforms define placement; shared materials define density, scattering and absorption.
# Assets/Volumes/SoftSphere.mktvol is the source density grid; saved material voxels are embedded.
# Play or Simulate advances the authored wind data; the game camera provides a repeatable viewpoint.

